> My main issues here are:
> 1) How do I get rid of my "burdened" state? I blessed my BoH (twice!), my
> Valkyrie is not so wimpy and I think I'm not carrying anything totally
> useless. I'm puzzled...

You must have more than you discussed above to be burdened. How's your 
STR? (You haven't been poisoned, have you?) Your bag of holding has been 
positively ID'd, right? If those two issues are not the problem, then 
you're just carrying too much stuff. Use up valuable scrolls like 
enchant armor, alchemize potions of full healing and quaff some of them. 
  Either ditch the gems (they're ultimately useless) or stash them 
somewhere to be picked up again on the Ascension Run if you want them 
for the final score. If you're like me, you hold on to way too many 
wands: most of the attack wands are essentially useless below the 
Castle. Anyway, the Castle is an excellent place to make a midgame 
stash. There is almost nothing you could bring that would be worth being 
burdened. It takes too much of a toll on speed.

> 2) Is my weaponry good enough to take on the critters down below?
> Should I get back to my stashes and resume Trollsbane, Ogresmasher and
> Cleaver? I feel really good with mojo and my faithful Vorpal Blade, but I
> don't know what to expect really.

Mojo is better than Vorpy, especially for Valks--higher average hp 
damage, and the beheading chance is less useful than it appears: you 
often end up beheading a monster you would have killed anyway.

Some people will tell you to go sacrifice for Grayswandir or Frost 
Brand; I'd say you're pretty well off with Mojo.

> 3) Is it safe to drink those 2 potions of gain level?

You're better off using them for alchemy. I also find it useful to curse 
  at least one; it helps for getting out of the Sanctum.

> 4) I'm well aware I need to make my armor a bit better, but I'd have to make
> the scrolls myself... Is is worth it?

Definitely. One of the main points of wishing for magic markers. At good 
enough AC, practically nothing hits you (with much damage, anyway).

> 5) How much should I donate to the priests to get clairvoyance? (money isn't
> an issue to me since I have all Ludios cleaned up and ready for looting)

200*XL (and has to be more than 1/3 of your visible money in inventory), 
but it only lasts for 500 to 999 turns. Plus, most people really don't 
want clairvoyance in Gehennom anyway. Makes it less clear where you've 
actually been and where you've just "seen" through clairvoyance. Scrolls 
of magic mapping are more useful.

